# I-Ching / Yilin graphics

Do not regress to a single hexagram slide that asserts “64” then jumps to 4,096.

Required sequence before Challenge:

1. Bits — `2¹=2` (yang | yin side by side, not stacked), `2³=8` (a trigram + the eight), `2⁶=64` (a 6-line hexagram, 蒙). Never claim 64 without drawing six lines.
2. 蒙 — worked hexagram only (“one of sixty-four”).
3. Pair — 井 48 → 渙 59, clay on changing lines, key `48-59`.
4. Grid — 64×64 matrix, cell 48–59 highlighted, `paintings[from][to]`.
5. Challenge — product job (paint every cell), not another combinatorics lesson.

Speak combinatorics, not cosmology. Do not put Shao Yong, qi, coins, or authorship on these slides. Gallery keys (`21→27`, `48-59`) are coordinates — do not re-explain hexagrams there.

Worked pair is always 井 48 → 渙 59 (overflowing well, already in the deck).
